  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement-I : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> -methylbutane on oxidation with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> -methylbutan-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-ol.</p><p>Statement-II : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> -alkanes can be easily oxidised to corresponding alcohol with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>Choose the correct option :</p>",
